<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bahia is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, which was the colonial capital of Brazil until 1763. It was a major destination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>, receiving many enslaved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba people</a> as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> collapsed in the nineteenth century. Yoruba religion and culture strongly shaped Afro-Brazilian traditions there, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/candomble">Candomblé</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bahia.jpg" alt="Bahia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diocleciano Ramos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_da_Bahia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
